50,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"A is cloud, B is modular, C is on-site, D is hosted. C's engineering team on-site sounds good for the yards.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,B's separate licenses are a red flag for my cost concerns. D's fixed configuration might be too rigid.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"A has a partner for migration, but D has a regional service team. I prefer a single point of support.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Rin,,"C is on our own servers, but I saw that we skip upgrades because it's too hard. A or D seems safer.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Servas,,"C's on-site team is tempting, but we have no admins left to help them. A's partner for training is a plus.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, if we go with A, will the partner actually help the supervisors, or just give a presentation?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Asuka, does D's fixed configuration mean the price stays flat, or will we pay for every single change?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, A's marketplace allows for flexibility. D is too rigid. I'm leaning toward A for the workflow options.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Rin,,I like A because it's a suite. No more mismatched pieces like in the 2018 move.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Servas,,A's partner handling the training and migration addresses my fear of the staff being stretched too thin.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm worried about A's ""configurable workflows"" being too complex for the yard. But C is too risky for the servers.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,A's subscription fits the board's preference for operating expenses over capital. I can support A.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Asuka,,A provides the best balance of a single platform with the ability to adjust as the business changes.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Rin,,A sounds like an adventure! Let's go with the Cloud Suite.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Servas,,I agree. The support for training and the cloud nature relieves the pressure on our dwindling admin staff.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'll go with A. It's better than the alternatives given our hardware and timing constraints.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
